      "technical_explanation": "The scanner flagged environment-variable access in a browser-based UI test harness. In context, the flagged function reads two environment variables that identify where a Chromium browser is installed, then uses those values to locate a local browser executable for the test runner to launch. The values are compared against the filesystem and used only as the launch target for the automated browser; they are never serialized into a payload, logged wholesale, persisted, or sent to any network destination. This is test automation infrastructure for locating a browser binary, not shipped extension behavior, and the small set of specific variables read is proportionate to that purpose. No exfiltration channel, obfuscation, or credential handling is present in the supplied evidence.",
